      "homepage": "https://github.com/IxMilia/dxf-rs",
      "rationale": "🖊️ THE CARRIER READER for note's DXF export, and already the qualifying reference `s.stdio.dxf@r12/✳️any` registers under `dxf-crate-r12-mutate` (this repository's `🔒️dependencies.json`) — reused here for the SAME crate reading the SAME `print_dxf_document` text this subset's own `NoteIntoDxf` serializer calls (`../🚪️io/📤️export/🧵️serializers/🗿️artifacts/🖊️dxf/🔖️r12/✳️any/🦀️component.rs`), so nothing new is being asked of `dxf` — only a second registration of an already-qualified crate against a second subset's vocabulary.\n\nWHAT IT CAN AND CANNOT WITNESS, read from the serializer's own body rather than assumed. `NoteIntoDxf::serialize` walks `flatten_blocks(&from.blocks)` and emits a `DxfEntity::Line` for every consecutive pair of an `Ink` block's OWN `points` array — nothing else: `if let NoteBlockNode::Ink { points, .. } = block { for pair in points.windows(2) { entities.push(DxfEntity::Line { start: [pair[0][0], pair[0][1], 0.0], end: [pair[1][0], pair[1][1], 0.0], layer: \"0\".into(), unknown_group_codes: Vec::new() }); } }`. Three consequences, each MEASURED against the serializer body rather than guessed: (1) `points` are written RAW, with no `block.x`/`block.y`/`rotation` transform applied anywhere in this function — so `move-block`, `drag-blocks`, `resize-block` and `move-block-to-container` produce byte-IDENTICAL DXF output regardless of the mutation; only `edit-block-ink-stroke` (which rewrites `points` itself) and existence changes (`create-block`/`delete-block`/`delete-blocks`/`duplicate-block`/`duplicate-blocks` when they add or remove an Ink block) are witnessable. (2) `flatten_blocks` is never filtered by `block_visible` here — unlike the SVG bridge below — so `change-block-visible`/`change-block-locked` leave the DXF output unchanged even though the block visually disappears in SVG; this is a genuine cross-carrier inconsistency in the subject, not a limitation of the oracle, and is reported rather than worked around. (3) the `Line` entity carries no width/color field, so `change-block-ink-width` is invisible here (it IS visible via the SVG carrier's stroke-width style). Every other block kind (Text/Image/Table/Math/Group) and every document-root setting (grid/snap/pencil/eraser/rename-note) never reaches this serializer at all.",
