      "homepage": "https://github.com/tafia/quick-xml",
      "rationale": "🎨️ THE RICHEST CARRIER for this subset. `NoteIntoSvg::serialize` (`../🚪️io/📤️export/🧵️serializers/🗿️artifacts/🎨️svg/🔖️1.1/✳️any/🦀️component.rs`) delegates to `note_document_to_svg`, a REAL bridge (never a hand-rolled string): `note_document_to_drawing_snapshot` (`../🚪️io/🦀️component.rs`) walks `flatten_blocks(&document.blocks).filter(|b| block_visible(b))` — visibility IS honoured here, unlike the DXF path above — and wraps every surviving block's shape in `DrawNode::Group { transform: note_block_transform(block), .. }`, where `note_block_transform` reads the block's OWN `x`/`y`/`rotation` into a real translate+rotate transform. `write_svg_xml` then prints that transform as the `<g transform=\"…\">` this probe reads back with quick-xml.\n\nPER-BLOCK-KIND WITNESSABILITY, read from `draw_node_from_note_block`. `Ink` → a real `<path>` (stroke geometry AND `stroke-width`, so `edit-block-ink-stroke` and `change-block-ink-width` are BOTH witnessable here, the second only here). `Text` → a real `<text>` element holding the joined paragraph text (`edit-block-text` witnessable) BUT `font_size` is wired to the glyph's `y` COORDINATE (`at: SemioPoint2 { x: 0.0, y: *font_size }`), never to a font-size style property — `change-block-font-size` therefore moves the baseline rather than changing any rendered size, a genuine subject bug this oracle exposes rather than one it can quietly confirm, so it is registered as unsupported/excluded from this mutation despite being numerically visible. `Image` → a real `<image>` with the asset's own bytes when the referenced asset exists (`create-asset`/`replace-asset-payload`/`delete-asset` witnessable ONLY when a visible Image block references that asset key), else a generic outline rectangle. `Table`/`Math`/`Group` → ALWAYS a generic gray outline rectangle keyed only to `width`/`height` — cell/formula CONTENT is invisible by construction (`edit-block-math` and the four table row/column verbs are un-witnessable here because their diffs mutate `rows`/`columns`/`cells`, never `width`/`height` — confirmed by reading `insert-table-row`'s own diff). `change-block-locked`, `rename-block` and `rename-note` have no rendered representation anywhere in this bridge.",
