      "rationale": "📄️ `lopdf` is ALREADY an approved test-oracle in this repository (`🔒️dependencies.json` — capabilities `pdf-edit`/`pdf-parse`, linked into the very crate `../../../../../../../../✏️s/🔌️plugins/🗄️stdio/🧪️oracle/📦️packages/🦀️rust/Cargo.toml` this registration reuses); this entry is a second registration of that crate against `note-1-mutate` rather than a new dependency.\n\n`NoteIntoPdf::serialize` (`../🚪️io/📤️export/🧵️serializers/🗿️artifacts/📄️pdf/🔖️1.4/✳️any/🦀️component.rs`) flattens the document's `title` (if any) followed by EVERY `Text` block's paragraph runs, space-joined, onto ONE `PdfPage.text` field of a single-page `PdfSnapshot` — real page geometry (`PageDoc`/`w`/`h`) and a real `encode_pdf`, never a stub. Two consequences read directly from that body: (1) `rename-note` IS witnessable here — the title is the first thing concatenated — even though it is invisible to both DXF and SVG. (2) exactly like the DXF path, `flatten_blocks` here is never filtered by `block_visible`, so `change-block-visible` on a Text block leaves the PDF text unchanged (the same cross-carrier inconsistency the DXF entry reports, independently confirmed on a second serializer). Position, block existence order beyond concatenation order, and every non-Text block kind (Ink/Image/Table/Math/Group) are invisible: the serializer never reads their fields at all.",
